  "theory": "\n<p class=\"callout\">📝 Der Test ist <b>auf Englisch</b> und hat <b>offene Fragen</b> – man muss frei formulieren, Beispiele geben und eine Zeitleiste zeichnen. Ankreuzen reicht hier nicht: Schreib deine Antwort zuerst selbst in das Feld und vergleich sie dann mit der Musterantwort.</p>\n\n<h3>1 · Routine work vs. project</h3>\n<table class=\"ops\">\n<tr><td></td><td><b>Routine work</b> (Routinearbeit)</td><td><b>Project</b> (Projekt)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>How often?</td><td>repeats again and again</td><td><b>unique</b> – done once (einmalig)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Time</td><td>ongoing, no fixed end</td><td><b>fixed start and end</b> (temporary)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Goal</td><td>keep the business running</td><td>a <b>specific, defined goal</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Resources</td><td>part of the normal budget</td><td><b>limited</b> budget, staff, time</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Know-how / risk</td><td>known procedures, low risk</td><td><b>new</b>, complex, <b>risky</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Organisation</td><td>normal line organisation</td><td><b>own temporary project organisation</b>, often interdisciplinary</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> Routine – changing the tyres of your car every year, the weekly server backup, sorting the mail every morning (always the same steps, no end, no risk). Project – developing a new website for a club, organising the school graduation party, migrating the school network (done once, fixed deadline and budget, new and complex).</p>\n\n<h3>2 · Failing project</h3>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"card\"><b>Reasons for failing</b><br>missing project management · incomplete or changing requirements · missing top-management support · wrong estimation of the initial situation · underestimated total work · bad cost monitoring · unrealistic time planning · unclear responsibilities · bad communication with the customer (Schaukel-Karikatur)</div>\n<div class=\"card\"><b>What to do better</b><br>tight project management · precise specification, agreed with the customer · detailed, realistic planning with buffers · realistic expectations · top-management support · clear roles and responsibilities · regular controlling (time, cost, quality) · risk analysis · regular meetings and reports with the customer</div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"tip\">💡 Trick für 2b: Nimm jeden Grund aus 2a und schreib das <b>Gegenteil</b> als Verbesserung dazu – die Erfolgsgründe sind die Gegenteile der Misserfolgsgründe.</p>\n\n<h3>3 · Project characteristics (at least four)</h3>\n<p><b>unique</b> (einmalig) · <b>clear goal</b> · <b>limited in time</b> (start + end) · <b>limited resources</b> (budget, staff) · <b>complex</b> · <b>risky</b> · <b>new / individual</b>, not routine · <b>interdisciplinary</b> team · <b>own temporary project organisation</b> · continuous dialogue between customer and contractor.<br>DIN 69 901: „Vorhaben, das im Wesentlichen durch Einmaligkeit der Bedingungen in ihrer Gesamtheit gekennzeichnet ist.“</p>\n\n<h3>4 · Environment analysis (Umfeldanalyse)</h3>\n<p>Collect <b>everyone outside the core team</b> who influences the project or is affected by it, and rate their attitude (positive / negative / conflict). Für <b>dein</b> IT-Projekt z.&nbsp;B.:</p>\n<table class=\"ops\">\n<tr><td><b>internal</b></td><td>project sponsor / customer (Auftraggeber), teachers / supervisors, school management, other classes and students as users, school IT administrator</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>external</b></td><td>suppliers (hosting, software licences, hardware), parents, data protection / authorities, partner companies, the public / media, competitors</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p class=\"tip\">💡 Im Test immer <b>konkret</b> auf das eigene Projekt beziehen (mit Namen bzw. Rollen) und kurz dazuschreiben, <b>warum</b> die Gruppe betroffen ist.</p>\n\n<h3>5 · Project phases – timeplan</h3>\n\n<div style=\"margin:16px 0 6px;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"min-width:560px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:0\">\n<div style=\"flex:1;padding:8px 6px;background:rgba(150,150,150,.12);border:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);text-align:center;font-size:13px\"><b>Vorprojektphase</b><br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">pre-project phase</span></div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;padding:8px 6px;background:rgba(70,130,220,.15);border:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);text-align:center;font-size:13px\"><b>Planungsphase</b><br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">planning phase</span></div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;padding:8px 6px;background:rgba(70,130,220,.15);border:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);text-align:center;font-size:13px\"><b>Realisierungsphase</b><br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">realisation phase</span></div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;padding:8px 6px;background:rgba(70,130,220,.15);border:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);text-align:center;font-size:13px\"><b>Abschlussphase</b><br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">final phase</span></div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;padding:8px 6px;background:rgba(150,150,150,.12);border:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);text-align:center;font-size:13px\"><b>Nachprojektphase</b><br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">post-project phase</span></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;font-size:12px;margin-top:4px\">\n<div style=\"flex:1\"></div>\n<div style=\"flex:3;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-top:3px solid #d33;padding-top:4px\">\n<span>▲ <b>offizieller Start</b><br>Projektauftrag unterschrieben</span>\n<span style=\"text-align:right\">offizielles <b>Ende</b> ▲<br>Abnahmeprotokoll / Abschlussbericht unterschrieben</span>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1\"></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;opacity:.75;margin-top:4px\">— eigentliches Projekt (rot) —</div>\n</div></div>\n<table class=\"ops\">\n<tr><td><b>Pre-project phase</b></td><td>idea, project request, feasibility study, rough planning → ends with the <b>project assignment</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Planning phase</b></td><td>tasks, specification, detailed planning, responsibilities, risk analysis</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Realisation phase</b></td><td>work on tasks, controlling, progress reports, milestones</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Final phase</b></td><td>acceptance of the product, final project report, reintegration of the team</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p class=\"callout\"><b>Official start</b> = when the <b>Projektauftrag</b> (project assignment) is <b>signed</b> by sponsor and project manager – between pre-project and planning phase.<br><b>Official end</b> = when the <b>Abnahmeprotokoll</b> (acceptance protocol) / <b>Projektabschlussbericht</b> (final report) is <b>signed</b> – at the end of the final phase. Die Vorprojektphase gehört noch <b>nicht</b> zum eigentlichen Projekt.</p>\n",
